+      "commit": "634bbd6732fc82f652eeb5c94d887904873f461a",
       "protected_paths": [
         "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp"
       ],
@@ -1831,7 +1831,7 @@
       "id": "qwen4exp-qsa-pooled-indexer-cache",
       "status": "active",
       "mechanism": "Persistent pooled indexer-key cache for qwen4exp QSA layers (Strata FEATURE-MAP row 25, lane 301). Pool + rms_norm + rope of the raw indexer keys runs ONCE per completed 4-cell block and is stored per QSA layer (f32 rows keyed by block index); each ubatch pools only its fresh blocks and the tail, instead of re-gathering, re-pooling, re-norming and re-roping all n_kv raw keys every token. Same op chain per row (bit-identical rows). Full pooling fallback (writes or marks stale) on multi-sequence, embedding ubatches with 2d positions, or spans past n_fresh; invalidation on clear/seq_cp/seq_keep/seq_add/seq_div/state_read. Switches: GGML_ARIFI_QSA_POOL_CACHE=0 (off == previous path), RED plant GGML_ARIFI_QSA_POOL_RED=2 (drops every fresh write).",
-      "commit": "13c3981eab31dc862899c029fe3cf746940708ab",
+      "commit": "ea75fe8cab01670aba413b794c4e170f696606e1",
       "protected_paths": [
         "src/llama-memory-hybrid-idx.cpp",
         "src/llama-memory-hybrid-idx.h",
@@ -1857,7 +1857,7 @@
       "id": "vulkan-cm1-f16b-staging-mul-mat-id",
       "status": "active",
       "mechanism": "coopmat1 (non-coopmat2, non-Intel) MUL_MAT_ID prompt matmuls stage B f32->f16 before the kernel (lane-296 N11 extended to the id path) when no int8 q8_1 id pipeline is taken and tokens >= cm1_f16b_min_n, so iq2_s / iq3_xxs / iq3_s experts run the f16-B coopmat1 pipeline instead of f32-B. Not a precision change on fp16 devices: the f32-B kernel already rounds B to f16vec2 in shared memory (mul_mm.comp:195). Default ON; GGML_ARIFI_CM1_F16B_ID=0 keeps f32-B; =red is the planted wrong variant (staged B never written).",
-      "commit": "75bd52ad79759c2ae3120a9209c6955e3c694246",
+      "commit": "1d7f47ec44f5383ffe892171a651312c8f765e84",
       "protected_paths": [
         "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp"
       ],
@@ -1882,12 +1882,12 @@
       "status": "active",
       "_registered": "2026-10-05, lane-302 (Opus 5.5). Registered as an OP-LEVEL win that shipped DEFAULT OFF. The served A/B (cellB-10051832) FAILED its pre-registered read rule (round 2 pairs -1.5..-2.8%, unbalanced order). Amended same day: the balanced served A/B (cellE-10052000, warm arm discarded, ABBA x2) PASSED its pre-registered default-on rule, so the gather is DEFAULT ON at width 1 from the flip commit (lane-302 branch, commit-msg-6).",
       "mechanism": "MUL_MAT_ID small-batch mat-vec (n_tokens 2..8) gets gather pipelines whose linear workgroup id maps to (row block = linear / nslots, slot = linear % nslots): consecutive workgroups are the routed slots of one weight row block, so slots that picked the same expert read that row block from L2 instead of DRAM. Per-workgroup math is unchanged (a permutation of work order), so output is byte-identical to the old path. GGML_ARIFI_MOE_GATHER unset = old path; =1 = slot-major gather (the measured width); =2/4 = multi-column variants that lose at real routing (padded-column ALU).",
